    "evidenceByGoal": "Weight loss/body-weight reduction and related anthropometric outcomes: (1) Phase 1b randomized, placebo-controlled, multiple-ascending-dose trial in Chinese adults aged 18–75 years with overweight or obesity; 24 participants were enrolled, with 8 assigned to mazdutide and 4 to placebo in each of two cohorts. Mazdutide was given subcutaneously once weekly for 12 weeks in the 9-mg cohort (3 mg during weeks 1–4, 6 mg during weeks 5–8, and 9 mg during weeks 9–12) and for 16 weeks in the 10-mg cohort (2.5 mg during weeks 1–4, 5 mg during weeks 5–8, 7.5 mg during weeks 9–12, and 10 mg during weeks 13–16), with placebo as comparator. Mean body-weight change was −11.7% versus −1.8% at week 12 in the 9-mg cohort and −9.5% versus −3.3% at week 16 in the 10-mg cohort; mazdutide also produced greater reductions in waist circumference and BMI. [22] Key limitation reported: the source states that a larger and longer phase 2 trial was needed. [22] (2) Phase 3 randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled GLORY-1 trial in 610 Chinese adults with overweight or obesity; participants received once-weekly subcutaneous mazdutide 4 mg, mazdutide 6 mg, or placebo for 48 weeks. Co-primary outcomes were percentage change in weight from baseline and achieving at least 5% weight reduction at week 32; mazdutide was superior to placebo for body-weight change, weight-loss targets, and multiple cardiometabolic risk factors. [23] Adverse-event discontinuation was reported as 1.5% with 4 mg, 0.5% with 6 mg, and 1.0% with placebo; the most frequent events were gastrointestinal and mostly mild to moderate. [24] Study-specific key limitation: not verified in reviewed source. (3) Randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase 1 trial in adults with overweight or obesity evaluating mazdutide up to 16 mg for safety and efficacy. Sample size, dose-escalation schedule, treatment duration, comparator details beyond placebo control, weight-loss results, adverse events, and study-specific key limitation: not verified in reviewed source.",
    "efficacyScore": 4,
