    "evidenceByGoal": "Goal: major depressive disorder (MDD), including depressive and cognitive symptoms. Design: Phase 1B, double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled, multiple-dose study with three cohorts [105]. Population: 24 patients with MDD; diagnosis and severity were confirmed through remote interviews [105]. Sample size: 24 total; cohort 1 received NSI-189 40 mg once daily (n=6) or placebo (n=2), cohort 2 received 40 mg twice daily (n=6) or placebo (n=2), and cohort 3 received 40 mg three times daily (n=6) or placebo (n=2) [105]. Dose: 40 mg once daily, twice daily, or three times daily [105]. Duration: 28 days of inpatient treatment, with outpatient follow-up through day 84 ±3 [105]. Comparator: placebo [105]. Outcome: exploratory measures included SDQ, MADRS, CGI-I, and MGH CPFQ; the source reports a promising reduction in depressive and cognitive symptoms, significant improvement in SDQ and CPFQ, medium-to-large effect sizes across measures, and persistence during follow-up [105]. Adverse events: NSI-189 was relatively well tolerated at all doses, with no serious adverse effects [105]. Key limitation: the main limitation was the small sample size of each cohort.",
