    "latestVerifiedPublicationYear": 2018,
    "humanStudyCount": 1,
    "totalStudyCount": 3,
    "evidenceByGoal": "Clinically active systemic lupus erythematosus resistant to or intolerant of conventional medications: one prospective, single-arm, open-label phase 1/2 human trial. Participants were adults with active systemic lupus erythematosus; 43 were enrolled, 3 were ineligible, and 40 were eligible. Sirolimus was started at 2 mg/day, adjusted for tolerance to maintain a 6–15 ng/mL therapeutic range, and given for 12 months. No comparator was used. Among the 29 patients who completed treatment, 16 (55%) had reduced disease activity; mean SLEDAI decreased from 10.2 to 4.8 and mean total BILAG index from 28.4 to 17.4 after 12 months, both with p<0.001. Mean daily prednisone use decreased from 23.7 mg to 7.2 mg after 12 months. Eleven of 40 eligible patients discontinued treatment because of intolerance (2) or non-compliance (9). Reported laboratory changes included moderate reductions in HDL cholesterol and haemoglobin and a possible reduction in neutrophils, while liver function and lymphocyte counts were unchanged. Key limitation: the study was single-arm and open-label, and the source states that placebo-controlled trials are needed; therefore, causal efficacy is not established. [129]",
    "efficacyScore": 2,
    "evidenceQualityScore": 2,
    "safetySummary": "In the verified lupus study, safety analyses included all patients receiving at least one dose. Eleven of 40 eligible patients discontinued treatment because of intolerance (2) or non-compliance (9). Liver function and lymphocyte counts were unchanged; HDL cholesterol and haemoglobin were moderately reduced, and neutrophil counts showed a moderate reduction that was not statistically significant in the supplied summary. The source states that these changes were considered safe within the observed range. No broader safety conclusion is verified from the reviewed records. [129]",
    "knownInteractions": "Not verified in reviewed sources. [129, 130, 131]",
    "regulatoryStatus": "Not verified in reviewed sources. [129, 130, 131]",
    "limitations": "Evidence is limited to one verified single-arm, open-label phase 1/2 study. The second record provides only an incomplete title and summary and is not verifiable for eligibility or outcomes; the third record is tagged as a review and is excluded by the audit rules. The verified study itself reports that placebo-controlled trials are warranted. [129]",
    "missingFields": "For the verified lupus study, a comparator was not used or not reported because the design was single-arm. Interaction data, regulatory status, and comparative efficacy were not verified in the reviewed sources. Detailed adverse-event frequencies beyond the reported intolerance-related discontinuations and laboratory changes were not provided in the supplied source. [129]",
