    "recordNumber": 220,
    "batchNumber": 4,
    "catalogId": "theacrine",
    "inputName": "Theacrine",
    "canonicalName": "Theacrine [207, 208, 209]",
    "aliases": "TeaCrine®, Teacrine™, 1,3,7,9-tetramethyluric acid [207, 208, 209]",
    "category": "purine alkaloid / dietary supplement ingredient [207, 208, 209]",
    "latestVerifiedPublicationYear": 2018,
    "humanStudyCount": 3,
    "totalStudyCount": 3,
    "evidenceByGoal": "Energy, mood, focus, and concentration: (1) Randomized three-period comparison in 20 healthy young adults (10 men and 10 women); TheaTrim containing branded theacrine (Teacrine™) plus caffeine 150 mg, caffeine 150 mg, or placebo, on three days separated by approximately one week, with assessments before and up to 4 hours after ingestion. The source reported no condition or interaction effects for trail making, digit-symbol substitution, or reaction time, but higher attentive, alert, focused, and energetic ratings and lower lethargic and groggy ratings with TheaTrim than placebo and caffeine. Adverse events: not verified in reviewed source; heart rate and blood pressure were largely unaffected. Key limitation: the source describes a single-dose/short-term study of healthy young adults and did not show statistically significant cognitive-performance improvement.\n\n(2) Two-part randomized human investigation in healthy participants: Part 1 included 9 participants taking 200 mg/day (n=6) or 400 mg/day (n=3) for 7 consecutive days, with visual-analog-scale assessments before and 1, 4, and 6 hours after ingestion; Part 2 included 15 healthy subjects receiving a single 200 mg dose or placebo in a double-blind, placebo-controlled crossover, assessed before and 1, 2, and 3 hours after ingestion. Energy, focus, and concentration increased from baseline in both Part 1 doses without a dose-response effect; after the single 200 mg dose, significant group-by-time interaction effects were reported for energy, fatigue, and concentration. Resting heart rate, gas exchange, systemic hemodynamics, and side-effect profiles did not change. Comparator: placebo in Part 2; Part 1 had no placebo comparator verified in the reviewed summary. Key limitation: small samples, short duration, subjective outcomes, and no verified clinical population. [208]\n\n(3) Randomized five-condition crossover in 50 healthy adults (24 men and 26 women), receiving placebo, theacrine 25 mg, theacrine 125 mg, caffeine 150 mg, or theacrine 125 mg plus caffeine 150 mg on five occasions separated by approximately one week; outcomes were subjective feelings, heart rate, blood pressure, and trail making at baseline and 2 and 4 hours, with vital-sign and subjective assessments through 5 hours. The source reported no condition effect for trail making and stated that caffeine and theacrine-plus-caffeine generally had the most favorable subjective scores, while 25 mg theacrine and placebo generally had the least favorable scores; theacrine alone at 125 mg or combined with caffeine did not significantly increase heart rate or blood pressure. Adverse events: not verified in reviewed source. Key limitation: acute study in healthy adults with subjective findings and no significant objective trail-making effect. [208]",
    "efficacyScore": 2,
    "evidenceQualityScore": 2,
    "safetySummary": "The reviewed sources reported that heart rate and blood pressure were largely unaffected in the TheaTrim study, that no changes in resting heart rate or side-effect profiles were noted in the two-part TeaCrine® study, and that 125 mg theacrine alone or with caffeine did not significantly increase heart rate or blood pressure in the five-condition study. Detailed adverse events and long-term safety were not verified in reviewed sources. [207, 208, 209]",
    "knownInteractions": "Caffeine coadministration was studied in two candidate records: one used theacrine-containing TheaTrim with caffeine 150 mg and compared it with caffeine 150 mg alone and placebo, and another included theacrine 125 mg plus caffeine 150 mg. A clinically meaningful interaction was not verified in reviewed sources. [209]",
    "regulatoryStatus": "Not verified in reviewed sources. [207, 208, 209]",
    "limitations": "The audit is restricted to the three supplied records and their summaries; formulation-specific evidence was not transferred between TheaTrim, TeaCrine®, and Teacrine®. The reviewed studies enrolled healthy adults, were acute or short-term, and did not establish clinical efficacy for a disease or medical condition. Adverse-event details, longer-term outcomes, and clinically relevant interaction data were not verified where not explicitly reported. [208] [208]",
    "missingFields": "Adverse events were not verified in the reviewed source summaries for records 1 and 3; clinical-population efficacy, longer-term outcomes, and detailed adverse-event reporting were not verified in the reviewed sources. [208] [208]",
