    "evidenceByGoal": "Weight management/body composition: one randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial studied 81 participants who completed 12 weeks during a calorie-restricted diet. The proprietary Phase 2 white kidney bean extract was given as 1,000 mg or 700 mg three times daily, 30 minutes before meals, with microcrystalline cellulose placebo. [213] The source reports dose-dependent reductions in body weight, fat mass, BMI, waist, hip, and, in the high-dose group, thigh circumference. [213] Adverse events and a key study limitation were not verified in the reviewed source; the summary only characterizes the product as safe. [213]\n\nStarch/glucose absorption: a separate record reports two single-dose human studies. [214] In one study, 11 fasting subjects consumed four slices of white bread and 42 g of margarine with or without 1.5 g of bean extract; glucose AUC-measured absorption was inhibited by 66%. [214] In the other, 7 subjects received 0.75 g of extract with a full meal, producing a non-significant 28–41% reduction in absorption, and the source reports a dose-response decrease in glucose absorption. [214] The duration beyond the single dose, adverse events, and a comparator for the 7-subject full-meal study were not verified in the reviewed source. Key limitation: these were small, acute studies, so longer-term clinical effects were not verified in the reviewed source. [214]",
