    "evidenceByGoal": "Cardiovascular risk factors in adults with diabetes: one randomized, placebo-controlled, double-blind, parallel-design trial in China enrolled 68 Chinese diabetic patients with at least one cardiovascular disease risk factor. [219] Bromelain was given at 1,050 mg/day as three 350-mg capsules for 12 weeks, compared with starch-filled placebo capsules. [219] The primary reported outcome was plasma fibrinogen: fibrinogen decreased by 0.13 g/L with bromelain versus 0.36 g/L with placebo, with no significant between-group difference. [219] Other reported outcomes—blood lipids, blood pressure, blood glucose, C-reactive protein, and anthropometric measures—also showed no statistically significant between-group differences. [219] Adverse events: not verified in reviewed source. Key limitation: baseline fibrinogen differences between groups despite randomization may have influenced the results. [219]",
    "efficacyScore": 2,
