    "latestVerifiedPublicationYear": 2026,
    "humanStudyCount": 2,
    "totalStudyCount": 3,
    "evidenceByGoal": "Verified human primary evidence was found for formulation-specific immune outcomes and healthy-aging biomarkers, but evidence cannot be transferred across formulations. Record 1: 12-week randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial in 80 adults aged 55–70 years of a colostrum-containing multi-nutrient supplement; dose was not verified in the reviewed source, comparator was placebo, and outcomes included immune/inflammatory markers, serum IGF-1, body composition, bone turnover, cognition, and safety. The supplement increased stool bovine IgG and serum IGF-1, while other parameters showed no significant changes. [228] Record 2: acute randomized, counterbalanced, double-blind placebo-controlled crossover trial in 16 healthy recreationally active males. Participants received bovine colostrum 30 g 1 hour before exercise, 5 g immediately before exercise, and 5 g midway through 2.5 hours of cycling, versus an isoenergetic placebo. Compared with placebo, bovine colostrum increased fMLP-stimulated blood neutrophil oxidative burst, salivary lysozyme, and bacterial-stimulated neutrophil elastase release, but had no effect on leukocyte trafficking, PMA-stimulated neutrophil oxidative burst, salivary secretory IgA, or salivary lactoferrin. [229] Duration beyond the acute exercise session was not verified in the reviewed source. Adverse events and key limitations were not reported for these trials in the reviewed summaries. Record 3 was not counted as a unique eligible primary study because it is titled as a product claim, has “All-Life Colostrum” as its author, lacks a DOI and venue, and aggregates descriptions of multiple separate studies rather than providing one verifiable primary record. [230]",
    "efficacyScore": 2,
    "evidenceQualityScore": 2,
    "safetySummary": "Record 1 reports that the colostrum-containing supplement was well tolerated, with no severe adverse events and mild, self-resolved gastrointestinal adverse events. [228] Adverse-event information for record 2 was not mentioned in the reviewed source.",
    "knownInteractions": "Not verified in reviewed sources. [228, 229, 230]",
    "regulatoryStatus": "Not verified in reviewed sources. [228, 229, 230]",
    "limitations": "Formulation-specific evidence cannot be pooled: record 1 concerns a colostrum-containing multi-nutrient supplement, whereas record 2 concerns acute bovine colostrum dosing. The reviewed summaries do not verify the dose for record 1, adverse events for record 2, or key study limitations for either eligible trial. Record 3 is an aggregated, non-verifiable product record and was assigned zero eligible studies. [228] [229] [230]",
