    "limitations": "Audit limited to the three supplied records for the exact catalogue input. No evidence was transferred across formulations or analogs. The geriatric record's supplied summary does not report sample size, dose, duration, comparator, outcomes, or adverse events. The postphlebitic-syndrome summary does not report sample size or duration and gives limited outcome detail. In the osteoporosis study, total body calcium and spinal-fracture findings favored treatment, while regional bone mass and bone-biopsy findings did not show significant differences. [395] [396] [397]",
