    "safetySummary": "In the HIV-associated weight-loss trial, treatment was generally well tolerated but was associated with significant increases in transaminases and low-density lipoprotein and decreases in high-density lipoprotein [398]. In boys with Klinefelter syndrome, reported safety-related findings included lower HDL cholesterol and more rapid advancement in bone age, alongside lower triglycerides [400]. Other adverse events and long-term safety were not verified in reviewed sources.",
